 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Thresholds (CI Integration)
+- `--threshold <metric>=<min>` CLI option allows reports to fail a CI job when metrics fall below specified minimums.
+- Metrics without scores (e.g., exact_match when no references provided) fail their thresholds instead of crashing.
+- Exit code 0 if all thresholds pass, 1 if any fail, 2 if threshold specification is invalid.
+- Reports include `passed` flag and `thresholds` array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` entries.
+- SDK: `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` array with the same validation.
+- Thresholds work with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`; only known metric IDs are accepted.
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
